---LINES
---SCREEN
=video attributes help

  /set "w"/ (write, output) is used when lines is shown
  /set "r"/ (read, input) is used when line is pointed by cursor (is active)
                            
  change an value:          
               .:SP...      
               .:DE...      ." logical type of lines : "................  
  change focus of input:      CMD - initial text mode (restored on exit)  
  switch w/r : .:KI....       TXT - text                                  
     set "w" : .'w or .'o     HDR - header                              
     set "r" : .'r or .'i     VAR - variable                              
                              ALT - alteratorction point                  
  change settings mode:       MSE - menu selection point                  
          .'0 .'1 .'2 .'3     ERR - error message                       
                              ATT - attention (warning message)         
                           
                           
---END
* line is a thing which links data and representation in variety of aspects
